            <ArticleTitle>Iliopsoas tendon dysfunction as a cause of pain after total hip arthroplasty relieved by surgical release.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>387-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain after total hip arthroplasty (THA) may be due to a number of factors, including dysfunction of the iliopsoas tendon. We report a case of persistent groin pain after THA. The pain was successfully treated using iliopsoas tenotomy rather than revision of any prosthetic component.</AbstractText>
